      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1887 Battle of Lewisham saw local residents defend the town against a mob, a rare civil‑defence episode in London.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewisham",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Goldsmiths College, founded as a technical institute in 1891, now belongs to the University of London and sits just outside Lewisham in New Cross.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Lewisham",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lewisham’s archives hold more than five centuries of history, with records dating back to 1476, available in the reading room at Catford Library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
